<p>Ultimately, you're doing yourself a disservice if you're lobbying people to refrain from downvoting despite their preferences. The goal here is to host works on this site that people want to read, not to prove a point.</p>
<p>If your goal is to have more screenplays on the site, then the best way to do that is to prove that they're a viable medium and write something that readers find entertaining. Having a screenplay hang around on the site even if people don't like it very much isn't going to prove that more people should write them.</p>
<p>Further, that may actually <em>dissuade</em> people from trying to do more of these, since the only extant example is hanging around in the negatives. Things are far simpler, and in my opinion better, if people just express their preferences on the piece rather than artificially trying to push something for its own sake.</p>

